From: MacGameVideoFix <https://github.com/MathiasKowoll/MacGameVideoFix>
Subject: [PATCH] winebus.sys: say which bus a device is on in its compatible ids

WHERE THIS CAME FROM

MacGameVideoFix's own series, mgvf-NNNN, written on 2026-09-08 after a day of
measuring why a DualSense rumbles over USB and never over Bluetooth in every
Steam game under CrossOver 26.3 on macOS. Nothing in it is specific to this
project; it is offered to anyone carrying a patched winebus.

THE FAULT

A DualSense on Bluetooth wants output report 0x31, 78 bytes with a CRC-32; its
Bluetooth descriptor has no report 0x02 at all (outputs 0x31..0x39, measured),
so the USB-format report a client sends is refused by hidclass before winebus
sees it, silently. Every Windows client decides USB against Bluetooth the same
way -- hidapi asks the HID device's parent devnode for its compatible ids and
searches them for BTHENUM -- and under wine that search can never succeed:
winebus reports WINEBUS\WINE_COMP_HID and WINEBUS\WINE_COMP_XINPUT and nothing
else, whatever the bus. Steam's own log records the result for a pad on
Bluetooth: "Added HIDAPI device 'DualSense Edge Wireless Controller' ...
bluetooth 0". Its PS5 driver then stays in simple mode and writes nothing;
over USB the same driver writes its 0x02 reports and the pad rumbles.

THE CHANGE

get_compatible_ids prepends the id a real Bluetooth HID child carries,
BTHENUM\{00001124-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb} (the Bluetooth HID service
class), when the device's bus_type is Bluetooth, and USB\Class_03 when it is
USB. WINE_COMP_XINPUT and WINE_COMP_HID follow as before, so nothing that
matched on them changes. winebus already knows the bus: bus_iohid.c reads the
IOKit Transport property into desc.bus_type, and it was used only for the PnP
device-id prefix and the Bluetooth input fixups.

Pairs with mgvf-0003, which gives CM_Get_Parent something to return; without
that, hidapi never reaches these ids.

---
--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c
+++ b/dlls/winebus.sys/main.c
@@ -262,17 +262,41 @@
 {
     static const WCHAR xinput_compat[] = L"WINEBUS\\WINE_COMP_XINPUT";
     static const WCHAR hid_compat[] = L"WINEBUS\\WINE_COMP_HID";
+    /* MGVF: say which bus the device is on, the way the Windows enumerators
+     * do. hidapi decides USB against Bluetooth by asking the HID device's
+     * parent devnode for its compatible ids and searching them for BTHENUM
+     * (or USB); with only WINE_COMP_* to look at, every controller reads as
+     * USB and a DualSense on Bluetooth is sent USB-format output reports it
+     * ignores. The GUID is the Bluetooth HID service class, which is what a
+     * real BTHENUM child carries. */
+    static const WCHAR bth_compat[] = L"BTHENUM\\{00001124-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb}";
+    static const WCHAR usb_compat[] = L"USB\\Class_03";
     struct device_extension *ext = (struct device_extension *)device->DeviceExtension;
-    DWORD size = sizeof(hid_compat);
+    const WCHAR *bus_compat = NULL;
+    DWORD size = sizeof(hid_compat), pos = 0;
     WCHAR *dst;
 
+    if (ext->desc.bus_type == BUS_TYPE_BLUETOOTH) bus_compat = bth_compat;
+    else if (ext->desc.bus_type == BUS_TYPE_USB) bus_compat = usb_compat;
+
+    if (bus_compat) size += (wcslen(bus_compat) + 1) * sizeof(WCHAR);
     if (ext->desc.is_gamepad) size += sizeof(xinput_compat);
 
     if ((dst = ExAllocatePool(PagedPool, size + sizeof(WCHAR))))
     {
-        if (ext->desc.is_gamepad) memcpy(dst, xinput_compat, sizeof(xinput_compat));
-        memcpy((char *)dst + size - sizeof(hid_compat), hid_compat, sizeof(hid_compat));
-        dst[size / sizeof(WCHAR)] = 0;
+        if (bus_compat)
+        {
+            wcscpy(dst + pos, bus_compat);
+            pos += wcslen(bus_compat) + 1;
+        }
+        if (ext->desc.is_gamepad)
+        {
+            memcpy(dst + pos, xinput_compat, sizeof(xinput_compat));
+            pos += ARRAY_SIZE(xinput_compat);
+        }
+        memcpy(dst + pos, hid_compat, sizeof(hid_compat));
+        pos += ARRAY_SIZE(hid_compat);
+        dst[pos] = 0;
     }
 
     return dst;
